language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Guards and apples: the boy passes num_gates gates; at each gate he gives the guard half his apples plus one, and the boy then gives his last apple to the girl.
given num_gates : int
$ apples[i] is the number of apples before gate i, and apples[num_gates+1] is the number left after the last gate; the reference bounds apples to 0..100
find apples : matrix indexed by [int(1..num_gates+1)] of int(0..100)
such that
$ one apple is left after the last gate; he gives it to the girl
apples[num_gates + 1] = 1,
$ at each gate the guard receives half the apples plus one, a whole number, so the apples before the gate are even; the apples after the gate are the apples before minus that bribe
forAll i : int(1..num_gates) . (apples[i] = 2 * apples[i + 1] + 2)
